---
import ProjectArticle from '@components/gta6-leonida-atlas/ProjectArticle.astro';
import { urls } from '@lib/urls';
---

<ProjectArticle
  path={urls.leonidaAtlasAbout()}
  title="About the atlas"
  section="Project"
  description="An independent attempt to make a changing body of GTA 6 location evidence legible, explorable and honest about its limits."
>
  <section>
    <h2>Why this exists</h2>
    <p>
      Public trailers, screenshots, official pages and community research reveal fragments of
      Leonida rather than a finished map. The atlas gives those fragments a shared frame so readers
      can inspect relationships without mistaking an estimate for confirmed geography.
    </p>
    <p>
      The project is editorial and evidentiary. It is not an official map, a leaked game asset or a
      promise that every road and landmark will appear in the released game.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>What “approximate” means</h2>
    <p>
      Community-derived coastlines, routes and positions can change when better evidence arrives.
      The experience keeps uncertainty visible and leaves unsupported areas unknown rather than
      completing them by guesswork.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Project status</h2>
    <p>
      The atlas is under active development. A public source release, contribution workflow and code
      license are in preparation; none has been published yet.
    </p>
  </section>
</ProjectArticle>
